A reverse-mode autograd engine in C, just big
enough to train karpathy's microGPT.


12 float64 ops record onto a tape that backward
walks in reverse. Memory is allocated statically,
TigerBeetle style: nothing is allocated after startup.


    $ make parity
    trained 1000 steps in 0.101s
    passed parity check (max |diff| 5.7e-15)
    inference (random sampled name): kaonle


Final weights match karpathy's microGPT to 1e-11.
Every op is also checked against finite differences.


References:

- autograd.lean: https://github.com/sueszli/autograd.lean
- microGPT: https://karpathy.github.io/2026/02/12/microgpt/
- TigerStyle: https://github.com/tigerbeetle/tigerbeetle/blob/main/docs/TIGER_STYLE.md
- Hacker News: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=46285424
